PART V - DISCLOSURES IN AND FILING OF LETTERS OF OFFER Disclosures in the draft letter of offer and letter of offer
	SEC 70. 
		SUBSEC (1)
			The draft letter of offer and letter of offer shall contain all material disclosures which are true and adequate to enable the applicants to take an informed investment decision.
			(2) Without prejudice to the generality of sub-regulation (1), the draft letter of offer and letter of offer shall contain disclosures as specified in {{^{{FOOTNOTE 141}}}}[Part B of Schedule VI].
			FOOTNOTE 141
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025 for the words, symbols and figures “Part B or Part B-1 of Schedule VI, as applicable”.
			(3) {{^{{FOOTNOTE 142}}}}[\*\*\*] (4) {{^{{FOOTNOTE 143}}}}[\*\*\*] (5)  The {{^{{FOOTNOTE 144}}}}[issuer] shall ensure that the information contained in the draft letter of offer and letter of offer and the particulars as per audited financial statements in the letter of offer are not more than six months old from the issue opening date.
			FOOTNOTE 142
				Omitted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025. Prior to its omission, sub-regulation (3) read as under,-
				“(3) The lead manager(s) shall exercise due diligence and satisfy themselves about all aspects of the issue including the veracity and adequacy of disclosure in the draft letter of offer and the letter of offer.”
			FOOTNOTE 143
				Omitted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025. Prior to its omission, sub-regulation (4) read as under,-
				“(4) The lead manager(s) shall call upon the issuer, its promoters and its directors to fulfil their obligations as disclosed by them in the draft letter of offer and letter of offer and as required in terms of these Regulations.”
			FOOTNOTE 144
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025 for the words and symbols “lead manager(s)”.
			(6)  An issuer shall make disclosures in the draft letter of offer {{^{{FOOTNOTE 145}}}}[and letter of offer], if the issuer or any of its promoters or directors is a {{^{{FOOTNOTE 146}}}}[wilful defaulter or a fraudulent borrower].
			FOOTNOTE 145
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025 for the words and symbol “, letter of offer and abridged letter of offer”.
			FOOTNOTE 146
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2022 w.e.f. 14.1.2022 for the words “wilful defaulter”.
			{{^{{FOOTNOTE 147}}}}[(7)  In  the  letter  of  offer  {{^{{FOOTNOTE 148}}}}[\*\*\*],  the  issuer  shall  disclose  the  process  of  credit  of  rights entitlements in the demat account and renunciation thereof.]
			FOOTNOTE 147
				Omitted by by the SEBI (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Sixth Amendment) Regulations, 2019 w.e.f. 26.12.2019.
