				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025 for the words and symbol “lead manager(s)”.
			(7)  In  case  of  undersubscribed  issues  that  are  underwritten,  the  {{^{{FOOTNOTE 210}}}}[designated  stock  exchange] shall  furnish  information  to  the  Board  in  respect  of  underwriters  who  have  failed  to  meet  their underwriting devolvement in the format specified in Schedule XVIII.
			FOOTNOTE 210
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025 for the words and symbol “lead manager(s)”. Release of subscription money
	SEC 94.  
		SUBSEC (1)
			The  {{^{{FOOTNOTE 211}}}}[issuer]  shall  confirm  to  the  bankers  to  the  issue  by  way  of  copies  of  listing  and trading approvals  that all formalities in  connection with  the issue have been completed and that the  banker  is  free  to  release  the  money  to  the  issuer  or  release  the  money  for  refund  in  case  of failure of the issue.
			FOOTNOTE 211
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 08.04.2025 for the words and symbol “lead manager(s)”.
			(2) In case the issuer fails to obtain listing or trading permission from the stock exchanges where the  specified  securities  were  listed,  it  shall  refund  through  verifiable  means  the  entire  monies received  within  {{^{{FOOTNOTE 212}}}}[four  days]  of  receipt  of  intimation  from  stock  exchanges  rejecting  the application for listing of specified securities,  and if any such money is not repaid within  {{^{{FOOTNOTE 213}}}}[four days] after the issuer becomes liable to repay it the issuer and every director of the company who is an officer in default shall, on and from the expiry of the {{^{{FOOTNOTE 214}}}}[fourth day], be jointly and severally liable to repay that money with interest at the rate of fifteen per cent. per annum.
			FOOTNOTE 212
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2022 w.e.f. 14.1.2022 for the words “seven days”.
			FOOTNOTE 213
