			SUBSEC vi.
				Net worth
			SUBSEC vii.
				Basic Earnings per share
			SUBSEC viii.
				Diluted Earnings per share
			SUBSEC ix.
				Return on net worth
			SUBSEC x.
				Net Asset Value per Share
			SUBSEC xi.
				Cash Flow Statements] {{^{{FOOTNOTE 724}}}}[\*\*\*] {{^{{FOOTNOTE 725}}}}[(11)  Business and Industry description:
				FOOTNOTE 724
					Omitted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 09.09.2025. Prior to omission, clause (12) read as follows, “(12) Management’s discussion and analysis of financial condition and results of operations”
				FOOTNOTE 725
					Renumbered and substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f. 09.09.2025. Prior to its renumbering and substitution, clauses (13) and (14) read as follows, “(13) Industry description (14) Business description”
				A summary of the primary business of the issuer and the industry in which it operates.]
				{{^{{FOOTNOTE 726}}}}[(12)] Organizational structure {{^{{FOOTNOTE 727}}}}[(13) Board of directors and senior management:
				FOOTNOTE 726
					Renumbered by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f.09.09.2025. Prior to its renumbering, it read as “(15)”.
				FOOTNOTE 727
					Renumbered and substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f.09.09.2025. Prior to its renumbering and substitution, clause (16) read as follows, “(16) Board of directors and senior management”
				Name, date of birth, age, Director Identification Number, address, occupation and date of expiration of the current term of office of manager, managing director and other directors (including nominee directors and whole-time directors).]
				{{^{{FOOTNOTE 728}}}}[(14)] Latest shareholding pattern as submitted to the stock exchange(s) {{^{{FOOTNOTE 729}}}}[(15)] Taxation aspects relating to the eligible securities {{^{{FOOTNOTE 730}}}}[(16) Outstanding litigation and legal proceedings:
				FOOTNOTE 728
					Renumbered by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f.09.09.2025. Prior to its renumbering, it read as “(17)”.
				FOOTNOTE 729
					Renumbered by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f.09.09.2025. Prior to its renumbering, it read as “(18)”.
				FOOTNOTE 730
					Renumbered and substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Second Amendment) Regulations, 2025 w.e.f.09.09.2025. Prior to its renumbering and substitution, clause (19) read as follows, “(19) Legal proceedings to be disclosed in accordance with the materiality policy framed under the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015”
		SEC 1.
			Summary of outstanding litigation and legal proceedings in a tabular format along with the amount involved, wherever quantifiable for the pending matters which, if they   result   in an   adverse   outcome, would   materially   and   adversely   affect the operations or the financial position of the issuer.
		SEC 2.
			Matters which are pending:
			SUBSEC i.
				Involving criminal liability on the part of the issuer. ii.  Material violations of the statutory regulations by the issuer. iii.  Economic offences where proceedings have been initiated against the issuer.
				For the purpose of determining materiality, the threshold shall be lower of threshold criteria mentioned below–
			SUBSEC i.
				As  per  the  policy  of  materiality  defined  by  the  board  of  directors  of  the  issuer  and disclosed in the placement document;
			SUBSEC ii.
				Litigation where the value or expected impact in terms of value, exceeds the lower of the following:
				PARA a)
					Two percent of turnover, as per the last audited consolidated financial statements of the issuer;
				PARA b)
					two percent of net worth, as per the last audited consolidated financial statements of the issuer, except in case the arithmetic value of the net worth is negative; or
				PARA c)
					five  percent  of  the  average  of  absolute  value  of  profit  or  loss  after  tax,  as  per  the  last three audited consolidated financial statements of the issuer.]
					{{^{{FOOTNOTE 731}}}}[(17)] Auditors {{^{{FOOTNOTE 732}}}}[(18)] General information {{^{{FOOTNOTE 733}}}}[(19)]  Such  other  information  as  is  material  and  appropriate  to  enable  investors  to  make  an informed investment decision.
