			SUBSEC (3)
				Terms of the Present Issue:
				• Issue details, including issue size • Names of stock exchanges where IDRs are proposed to be listed • Designated stock exchange • Procedure • Indicative timeline
			SUBSEC (4)
				Instructions for Applicants:
		SEC (a)
			How to apply, availability of prospectus, abridged prospectus and application forms, mode of payment and book building procedure, if relevant.
		SEC (b)
			In the application form,  the declaration relating to nationality and residency shall be shown prominently as under:
			"Nationality and Residency (Tick whichever is applicable)
				PARA (i)
					I am/We are Indian National(s) resident in India and I am/We are not applying for the said equity shares as nominee(s) of any person resident outside India or Foreign National(s).
				PARA (ii)
					I am/We are Indian National(s) resident in India and I am/We are applying for the said equity shares as Power of Attorney holder(s) of Non- Resident Indian(s) mentioned below on non-repatriation basis.
				PARA (iii)
					I am/We are Indian National(s) resident outside India and I am/We are applying for the said equity shares on my/our own behalf on non-repatriation basis."
		SEC (c)
			The  application  form  should  contain  necessary  instructions/provisions  for  the following:
				PARA (i)
					Instructions  to  applicants  to  mention  the  number  of  application  form  on  the reverse of the instruments to avoid misuse of instruments submitted along with the applications for shares/debentures in public issues.
				PARA (ii)
					Provision  in  the  application  form  for  inserting  particulars  relating  to  bank account number and the name of the bank with whom such account is held, to enable  printing  of  the  said  details  in  the  refund  orders  or  for  refunds  through Electronic Clearing System.
				PARA (iii)
					Instruction  to  applicants  to  disclose  Permanent  Account  Number  in  the application form, irrespective of the amount for which application/bid is made, along with the instruction that applications without Permanent Account Number would be rejected.
				PARA (iv)
					PAN/GIR number.
				PARA (v)
					Details  of  options,  if  any,  to  receive  securities  subscribed  for  and  a  statement that  trading  in  securities  on  the  stock  exchanges  in  physical  form  will  be available only subject to limits prescribed by the Board.
		SEC (d)
			Any  special  tax  benefits  for  issuing  company  and  its  shareholders  (Only  section numbers  of  the  Income  Tax  Act  and  their  substance  should  be  mentioned,  without reproducing the text of the sections).
		SEC (e)
			Restrictions on investments in IDRs/fungibility of IDRs.
			SUBSEC (5)
				Particulars of the Issue:
		SEC (a)
			Objects of the issue
		SEC (b)
			Project cost
		SEC (c)
			Means of financing
		SEC (d)
			Name of the Appraising Agency, if any
		SEC (e)
			Name of the Monitoring Agency, if any
	SUBPART - (6)  Description of the IDRs and Rights of IDR Holders:
		SEC (a)
			Brief description of the IDRs
		SEC (b)
			Dividends, other distributions and rights of IDR holders
		SEC (c)
			Voting rights and their manner of exercise by IDR holders, if any
		SEC (d)
			Record dates and how the same will be disclosed
		SEC (e)
			Reports and other communication to which the IDR holders will be entitled
		SEC (f)
			Conversion procedure of IDRs into shares
		SEC (g)
			Governing law regarding various aspects of IDRs and transactions therein.
			SUBSEC (7)
				Business Model/ Business Overview and Strategy (500 word limit in total)
	SUBPART - (8)  Exchange-wise stock market data:
		This  information  should  updated  as  on  the  last  available  date  before  the  date  of  the prospectus
		SEC (a)
			Market price of shares for each quarter of the last three calendar  years preceding the calendar  year preceding the  year of the issue of the prospectus  (High,  Low, Average Daily Trading Volume)
		SEC (b)
			Market price of shares for each month of the calendar  year preceding the year of the
	SUBPART - issue of the prospectus (High, Low, Average Daily Trading Volume)
		SEC (c)
			Market price of shares for the month preceding the date of the prospectus (High, Low, Average Daily Trading Volume)
		SEC (d)
			The Opening and Closing price on the last day of the preceding month of the date of the prospectus along with the volume
			SUBSEC (9)
				Internal Risk Factors: Minimum 5 and maximum 10 risk factors to be specified (500 word limit in total)
	SUBPART - (10)  Outstanding Material Litigations and Defaults
		SEC A.
			Total number of outstanding litigations against the company and amount involved
		SEC B.
