	SUBPART - (1)  Changes which require fresh filing of the draft offer document with the Board, along
	SUBPART - with fees:
		If changes are made in the offer document with respect to any of the following, the issuer
		shall  file  fresh  draft  offer  document  with  the  Board  in  terms  of  applicable  provisions  of
		these regulations, along with the fees as specified {{^{{FOOTNOTE 777}}}}[Schedule III]:
		FOOTNOTE 777
			Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2022 w.e.f. 14.1.2022 for the word and symbol “Schedule IV”.
		SEC (a)
			Change in promoter of the issuer.
		SEC (b)
			Change in more than half of the board of directors of the issuer.
		SEC (c)
			Change in main object clause of the issuer.
		SEC (d)
			Any addition to objects of the issue resulting in an increase in the estimated issue size or estimated means of finance by more than twenty per cent.
		SEC (e)
			If  there  are  grounds  to  believe  that  there  is  an  exacerbation  of  risk  on  account  of deletion of an object resulting in a decrease in issue size by more than twenty per cent
		SEC (f)
			{{^{{FOOTNOTE 778}}}}[ Any Increase or Decrease:
			FOOTNOTE 778
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2018 w-e-f- 31.12.2018. Prior to its substitution, sub-clause (f) read as follows,-
				“(f) Any increase or decrease in estimated issue size by more than twenty per cent.”
			SUBSEC (i)
				In  case  of  a  fresh  issue:  any  increase  or  decrease  in  estimated  issue  size {{^{{FOOTNOTE 779}}}}[(in Rupee value)] by more than twenty per cent. {{^{{FOOTNOTE 780}}}}[\*\*\*]; or
				FOOTNOTE 779
					Inserted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2024 w.e.f. 18.05.2024.
				FOOTNOTE 780
					The words “of the estimated issue size” omitted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2024 w.e.f. 18.05.2024.
			SUBSEC (ii)
				In case of an offer for sale: any increase or decrease in either the number of shares  offered  for  sale  or  the  estimated  issue  size  {{^{{FOOTNOTE 781}}}}[(in  Rupee  value), whichever  is  disclosed  in  the  draft  offer  document],  by  more  than  fifty  per cent.; or
				FOOTNOTE 781
					Inserted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2024 w.e.f. 18.05.2024.
			SUBSEC (iii)
				In case of an issue comprising of both fresh issue and offer for sale: the respective limits as above shall apply.]
		SEC (g)
			Any increase in estimated deployment in any of the objects of the issue by more than twenty per cent.
			Changes which may result in non-compliance with the provisions of the Securities and Exchange Board  of  India  (Issue  of  Capital  and  Disclosure  Requirements)  Regulations,  2018  and  the  lead manager(s) or issuer do not intend to seek relaxation under regulation 303 of the said regulations.
	SUBPART - (2)  Changes  which  require  filing  of  the  updated  offer  document  with  the  Board,  along
	SUBPART - with fees:
		SEC (a)
			If changes are made in  the offer document with  respect  to  any of the following, the issuer  shall  file  an  updated  offer  document  with  the  Board  ,  along  with  payment  of fees as specified in {{^{{FOOTNOTE 782}}}}[Schedule III]
			FOOTNOTE 782
				Substituted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2022 w.e.f. 14.1.2022 for the word and symbol “Schedule IV”.
			SUBSEC (i)
				Section  1:  Risk  Factors:  Any  material  development  which  may  result  in potential risk and may require updation in this section.
			SUBSEC (ii)
				Section 2: Capital Structure: An aggregate increase of 5 per cent. or more in the shareholding of the promoter or promoter group or an aggregate increase of
				PARA 5
					per cent. or more in the shareholding of the top ten shareholders.
		SEC (iii)
			Section  3:  Issue  Size:  Any  addition  or  deletion  to  the  objects  of  the  issue resulting in a change in the estimated issue size or estimated means of finance by more than 10 per cent. and not exceeding 20 per cent.
		SEC (iv)
			Section 4: Management: Appointment of any new director.
		SEC (v)
			Section  5:  Promoter  Group:  Any  addition  to  the  promoter  group  or  group companies.
		SEC (vi)
			Section  6:  Financial  Statements:  Any  variation  in  net  profit  after  tax  or  net loss and/ or extraordinary items in excess of 10 per cent. over the last updated financials included in the draft offer document.
		SEC (vii)
			Section  7:  Legal  and  other  information:  Any  new  litigation  or  any development about a pending litigation which is considered material by the lead manager(s).
			SUBSEC (a)
				After filing the updated offer document with the Board, the issuer may proceed with the issue after receiving a confirmation to this effect from the Board.
	SUBPART - (3)  Changes which require filing of the updated offer document with the Board, without
		fees:
		All other changes or updations in the offer document which are not covered under paras (1) and  (2)  above  shall  be  carried  out  in  the  offer  document  and  the  updated  offer  document shall be filed with the Board, without any fees.
	SUBPART - {{^{{FOOTNOTE 783}}}}[SCHEDULE XVI-A - NATURE OF CHANGES IN THE OFFER DOCUMENT
		FOOTNOTE 783
			Inserted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Fourth Amendment) Regulations, 2022, w-e-f 21.11.2022.
	SUBPART - REQUIRING FILING OF UPDATED OFFER DOCUMENT
	SUBPART - [See regulation 59E (2)]
	SUBPART - (1)  Changes which require fresh filing of the pre-filed draft offer document or draft offer
	SUBPART - document with the Board, along with fees:
		SEC (a)
			If  changes  are  made  in  the  pre-filed  draft  offer  document  after  receipt  of  observations  or comments from the Board with respect to any of the following, the issuer shall file the fresh pre-filed  draft  offer  document  or  draft  offer  document  with  the  Board  in  terms  of  the applicable provisions of these regulations, along with the fees as specified in Schedule III:
			SUBSEC (i)
				Change in the promoter of the issuer.
			SUBSEC (ii)
				Change in more than half of the board of directors of the issuer.
			SUBSEC (iii)
				Change in the main objects clause of the issuer.
			SUBSEC (iv)
				Any addition to the objects of the issue resulting in an increase in the estimated issue size or estimated means of finance by more than fifty per cent.
			SUBSEC (v)
				If there are grounds to believe that there is an exacerbation of risk on account of deletion of an object resulting in a decrease in issue size by more than fifty per cent.
			SUBSEC (vi)
				In case of a fresh issue, any increase or decrease in the estimated issue size {{^{{FOOTNOTE 784}}}}[(in Rupee value)]  by more than fifty percent.
				FOOTNOTE 784
					Inserted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2024 w.e.f. 18.05.2024.
			SUBSEC (vii)
				In case of an offer for sale, any increase or decrease in the number of shares offered for sale  or  the  estimated  issue  size  {{^{{FOOTNOTE 785}}}}[(in  Rupee  value),  whichever  is  disclosed  in  the  draft offer document],  by more than fifty percent.
				FOOTNOTE 785
					Inserted by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) (Amendment) Regulations, 2024 w.e.f. 18.05.2024.
			SUBSEC (viii)
				In  case  of  an  issue  comprising  of  both  fresh  issue  and  offer  for  sale,  any  increase  or decrease in the respective limits as specified in clause (vi) and clause (vii).
			SUBSEC (ix)
				Any  increase  in  estimated  deployment  in  any  of  the  objects  of  the  issue  by  more  than twenty per cent.
		SEC (b)
			Changes  which  may  result  in  non-compliance  with  the  provisions  of  the  Securities  and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2018 and the  lead  manager(s)  or  issuer  do  not  intend  to  seek  relaxation  under  regulation  303  of  the  said regulations.
	SUBPART - (2)  Changes  which  require  filing  of  the  updated  pre-filed  offer  document  with  the  Board,
	SUBPART - along with fees:
		SEC (a)
			If changes are made in the pre-filed offer document with respect to any of the following, the issuer  shall  file  an  updated  offer  document  with  the  Board,  along  with  payment  of  fees  as specified in Schedule III:
			SUBSEC (i)
				Section 1: Risk Factors: Any material development which may result in potential risk and may require updation in this section.
			SUBSEC (ii)
				Section  2:  Capital  Structure:  An  aggregate  increase  of  5  percent  or  more  in  the shareholding of the promoter or promoter group or an aggregate increase of 5 per cent. or more in the shareholding of the top ten shareholders.
			SUBSEC (iii)
				Section 3: Issue Size:  Any  addition  or deletion to  the objects  of the issue resulting in  a change in the estimated issue size or estimated means of finance by more than 10 percent and not exceeding 20 per cent.
			SUBSEC (iv)
				Section 4: Management: Appointment of any new director.
			SUBSEC (v)
				Section 5: Promoter Group: Any addition to the promoter group or group companies.
			SUBSEC (vi)
				Section  6:  Financial  Statements:  Any  variation  in  net  profit  after  tax  or  net  loss  and/  or extraordinary items in excess of 10 percent over the last updated financials included in the draft offer document.
			SUBSEC (vii)
				Section 7: Legal and other information: Any new litigation or any development about a pending litigation which is considered material by the lead manager(s).
		SEC (b)
			After filing the updated offer document with the Board, the issuer may proceed with the issue after receiving a confirmation to this effect from the Board.
	SUBPART - (3)  Changes  which  require  filing  of  the  updated  offer  document  with  the  Board,  without
	SUBPART - fees:
		All other changes or updations in the pre-filed offer document which are not covered under paras
				PARA (1)
					and (2) above shall be carried out in the offer document and the updated offer document shall be filed with the Board without any fees.]
